---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { u } from '../../../lib/paths';
---

<Base title="Read a billing statement" description="How University of Mars student bills are organized and how to ask about a charge.">
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Billing"
    title="Read a billing statement"
    lede="The cashier posts charges in MyUM. Aid for 2026–27 pays after you accept the award and any hold is cleared."
    crumbs={[
      { href: '/support/', label: 'Student Support' },
      { href: '/support/articles/billing/', label: 'Billing' },
    ]}
  />
  <article class="prose wrap narrow">
    <p>The statement has three blocks: tuition and fees, housing and meals, and other charges such as a lab fee or a library fine. A credit from aid appears as a payment, not as a lower tuition line.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Fall Semester charges posted in August 2026. Spring Semester charges posted in December 2026.</li>
      <li>A payment plan splits the remaining balance into four monthly payments. Join in the first two weeks of the term if you have not already.</li>
      <li>Refunds of a credit balance go to the bank account on file about ten business days after aid disburses.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      A past-due balance can place a bursar hold. That hold is separate from a financial aid hold. If a line looks wrong,
      submit a billing request and include the charge date and the amount.
    </p>
    <p class="page-actions">
      <a class="btn" href={u('/support/?category=billing#request')}>Ask about a charge</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
